================================================================================
r141 -- sizing r140 option (a): the consumer-side honest-algebra re-gate
RAN (executed on-box; numbers re-read from on-disk bb 5.1.0 output JSON)
================================================================================

SETUP
  Round base : git HEAD c79782a (r140); origin/main 62cc527, 0 rebase (no-op).
  Preset     : N_parts=19 T=9, L=2, QIS=61, BIT_MSG=58, BIT_SHARE=58, H=14
  Locked by a 2-line sed flip of committed mod.nr (insecure -> secure),
  byte-verified before and after the sweep; restored to committed after.
  4-core taskset, bb 5.1.0 noir-recursive-no-zk, nargo 1.0.0-b26.

6-LEG GATE TABLE (secure-8192, circuit_size + acir_opcodes)
  LEG         K   circuit_size   acir_ops
  base       6      16,409          6      (r137 committed w6 anchor)
  base      12      32,801         12      (r137 committed w12 anchor)
  e_par      6      68,429                 (this round: base + 1 parity row)
  e_par     12     133,999                 (this round)
  e_range    6     387,792       147,462   (this round: base + per-coeff range)
  e_range   12     772,824       294,924   (this round)

Wall-clock per prove (4-core): base ~54s, e_par ~90s, e_par12 ~150s,
e_range ~150s, e_range12 ~280s. Sweep total ~12 wall, in budget.

WHAT WAS MEASURED
  Each circuit is one consumer self-check block with K cells (K=6 or 12):
  reverse -> digest-flatten (Pollard const 3641542188856621199) -> acc-pin,
  then one add-on:
    e_par   : one parity row  (sum h[0]*payload[j] == 0 mod q)
    e_range : per-coefficient  NumberCheck(1 << 58)  on each coefficient
  This is a kernel-shape probe, not the full production consumer (no
  19-party assert side, no H=14 walker). It measures incremental gates
  for the add-on at fixed N=8192, H=14.

PROVENANCE (what makes the numbers trustworthy)
  1. base K=6 = 16,409  digit-twins committed r137 w6_gates.json.
     base K=12 = 32,801 digit-twins committed r137 w12_gates.json.
  2. K=6 -> K=12 ratio uniform ~2.0x across all three arms
     (2.00 / 1.96 / 2.00) -> all five compiled under one preset.
  3. e_range K=6 re-run twice, identical 387,792 / 147,462 both times.

INCREMENTAL DELTAS (add-on over the w-class base, same K)
  K=6 :  parity row = 68,429 - 16,409 =  52,020 g   (4.17x base cell)
         range add  = 387,792 - 16,409 = 371,383 g  (23.63x base cell)
  K=12:  parity row = 133,999 - 32,801 = 101,198 g   (4.09x base cell)
         range add  = 772,824 - 32,801 = 740,023 g  (23.56x base cell)

HEADLINE (RAN-robust)
  The r140 acc-pin cell is not kernel-closed; closing it needs at least a
  per-cell parity row. That costs 4.17x (K=6) / 4.09x (K=12) the cell.
  The full per-coefficient range family costs 23.63x / 23.56x the cell.

WHY NO H=14 PRODUCTION NUMBER HERE
  The production H=14 consumer cell (19-party walker) was never RAN in the
  r137 reference or this sweep; no on-disk file holds that number. r143
  must reconstruct the full consumer iterates at H=14 and re-run.

VERDICT
  The "re-gate is free" framing is now sized: parity-only = 4x the cell,
  range-line = 23.6x the cell. Parity-only is ~5x cheaper per cell.
  Owner call for r142: parity-only vs range-line (does the closure need
  range-checks, or can they move off the consumer path?).

